# Gemma 4 26B — AILANG-eval-tuned variant
#
# Why this variant exists: Google's default Gemma 4 sampling params
# (temperature=1.0, no repetition penalty) cause occasional token-collapse
# loops in agentic tool-call scenarios. Empirically observed 2026-05-23:
# gemma4:26b emitted the string `v_h_y_f_d_` 32,000 times in a single
# write-tool filePath argument, burning 9 minutes of GPU time. See the
# upstream bug at https://github.com/google-deepmind/gemma/issues/622
# ("Gemma 4 token repetition collapse … affects 31b Dense and 26b MoE").
#
# The OpenAI-compatible /v1/chat/completions endpoint does NOT pass through
# `top_k`, `repeat_penalty`, `min_p`, `num_predict` (per Ollama OpenAI
# compatibility docs). They MUST be set in a Modelfile to actually take
# effect. The opencode.jsonc sets the OpenAI-compat names (temperature,
# top_p, frequency_penalty, max_tokens) which DO pass through.
#
# Build:    ollama create gemma4:26b-ailang -f tools/ollama/gemma4-26b-ailang.modelfile
# Verify:   ollama show gemma4:26b-ailang --modelfile
# Use:      reference as `gemma4:26b-ailang` in opencode + models.yml

FROM gemma4:26b

# Google official top-k for Gemma 4 (Ollama gemma4:26b params blob).
PARAMETER top_k 64

# Community consensus value for agentic tool-call loops with Gemma 3/4
# (mychen76/gemma3_cline_roocode_qat ModelFile, Ollama issue #15502 mitigation).
# Kept at 1.1, NOT higher, because smcleod.net 2025-04 LLM sampling guide
# notes >1.1 hurts code because variable names should legitimately repeat.
PARAMETER repeat_penalty 1.1
PARAMETER repeat_last_n 256

# Safety-floor under top_p. Unsloth's Gemma run guide notes min_p=0.01
# "works well"; we use 0.05 as a slightly stricter floor for agentic loops.
PARAMETER min_p 0.05

# Cap any single generation at 4096 tokens. The repetition-collapse incident
# emitted 32,000 tokens in one tool argument. Even with sampling fixes,
# this is a hard belt-and-suspenders backstop.
PARAMETER num_predict 4096
